    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="0754" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ib3/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Queenstown</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 31,
                            1915, 8.20 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Burns changes statement. Says submarine fired two shots before ship<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d721-f1"/> sought to stop, then several more before submarine, which
                    was dead astern, appeared to realize ship had stopped.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d721-f1" n="1" xml:id="d721-f1-content">
                <p>See the case of the <hi rendition="#italic">Iberian, ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg492">p. 492</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
